+# Menu system: settings menus, graphics tech, input switching, graphs, the Menu Manager
+
+> **Standing expectation (the user's own words):** "There could be more use cases that users desire that I haven't thought of, but would be expected in a production-grade application." The section *Beyond the request* lists what was added for it; *Still open* lists what is still expected and not done.
+
+## Asked
+"Menu system: out of the box integration with Nvidia and AMD for things like DLSS or FSR; plumbing for many common graphics settings like Vsync with easy extensibility for custom settings like Render Distance; plumbing for many common accessibility settings; easy input switching; runtime graph widget (modular) - can easily be used for common benchmarking, like fps, gpu/cpu frametime; AI creation support e.g. "Create me a settings menu with the tabs: controls, video, audio and accessibility, use a simple style binded to data asset(s) so I can easily configure its look"; anything else that is key for menu tooling for easy and modularity in creating game menus." And: "If the menu manager is insufficient, or not at an out of the box AAA standard, feel free to work that as well."
+
+## What production menus do (the research this is built on)
+- **Settings as data, not screens.** Lyra's GameSettings plugin: a registry of setting objects (discrete, scalar, action, collections / pages), each with edit conditions (enable / visible, with a reason), dependencies (one setting re-evaluates others), a value source split between machine settings (`GameUserSettings`: display, scalability) and per-user shared settings (save game), and screens generated from it with a description panel. Here: Settings Schema assets + a per-player subsystem; the built-in pages ship in code.
+- **Apply, confirm, revert.** PC games stage display changes and ask "Keep these settings? Reverting in 15 s" (Windows' own pattern); consoles apply instantly. Unapplied changes are asked about on Back. Reset to defaults per page. Here: an Apply policy per screen, a confirmation countdown for flagged settings, Revert to the session start, Reset Page.
+- **Vendor tech through the vendors' Unreal plugins.** NVIDIA ships DLSS (Super Resolution, DLAA, Ray Reconstruction) and Streamline (Frame Generation, Reflex); AMD ships FidelityFX FSR (upscaling, frame interpolation) and Anti-Lag 2; Intel ships XeSS (upscaling, XeSS-FG, XeLL). All are driven by console variables, and their Blueprint libraries answer "supported on this GPU?". Games show only what the card supports, with Auto picking DLSS on RTX, FSR on AMD, XeSS on Intel, TSR otherwise. Modes are fixed render ratios (Quality 1.5x, Balanced 1.7x, Performance 2x, Ultra Performance 3x; DLAA / Native AA 1x).
+- **Accessibility** (Xbox Accessibility Guidelines, Game Accessibility Guidelines, CVAA): colour blindness filters (Slate's colour vision correction, as Lyra), text / UI size, subtitles (size, background, speaker names), reduce motion, flashing reduction, camera shake, toggle instead of hold, remapping every input, screen-reader narration of menus (XAG 104), notification time.
+- **Input switching.** CommonUI's input pre-processor: the last device used (with thresholds against a resting mouse or a drifting stick) switches the input method and the gamepad family (Xbox / PlayStation / Switch prompts) from the hardware the platform reports; prompts follow; the cursor hides on a pad; focus is given back to the screen for pad navigation.
+- **Rebinding** through Enhanced Input's user settings (player mappable keys, key profiles, slots), with conflict handling (swap / unbind / refuse), reserved keys, a "press a key" capture with cancel and timeout.
+- **Performance overlays and benchmarks** (stat unit, RTSS, CapFrameX, in-game benchmarks): fps, frame time and per-thread times graphed, average fps and 1% / 0.1% lows, percentiles, hitches, a CSV.
+
+Sources: Lyra `GameSettings` / `LyraSettingsLocal` / `LyraSettingsShared` (edit conditions, Apply / Revert, safe-zone and colour-blind settings, `SetColorVisionDeficiencyType`), CommonUI `FCommonInputPreprocessor` / `UCommonInputSubsystem` / platform gamepad names, Enhanced Input `UEnhancedInputUserSettings` (5.3+), NVIDIA DLSS / Streamline UE plugin docs (`r.NGX.DLSS.*`, `r.Streamline.DLSSG.*`, `t.Streamline.Reflex.*`), AMD FSR 3 UE plugin docs (`r.FidelityFX.FSR3.*`, `r.FidelityFX.FI.Enabled`), Intel XeSS UE plugin docs (`r.XeSS.*`), Xbox Accessibility Guidelines.
+
+## Files (`Plugins/NameTBD/Source/NameTBD/Menu/`)
+- `MenuManagerComponent.h/.cpp`, `MenuTypes.h`, `MenuScreenInterface.h`: the Menu Manager (below). `MenuPlayerUtils.h/.cpp`: whose menus (player from a context), the playing world for console commands.
+- `Settings/`: `MenuSettingTypes` (kinds, scopes, conditions, options, `FMenuImage`, value text helpers, `LogNameTBDSettings`), `MenuSetting` (`UMenuSetting` and Bool / Number / Choice / KeyBinding / Action / Info), `MenuSettingTargets` (where values go; `MenuAccessibility` flags), `MenuSettingsSchema` (`UMenuSettingsSchema` data asset, pages, sections, merging), `MenuSettingsDefaults` (the built-in pages), `MenuSettingsSubsystem` (`UMenuSettingsSubsystem`, `UMenuSettingsSaveGame`, console commands), `MenuProjectSettings` (Project Settings > Plugins > Menus), `MenuSettingsLibrary` (Blueprint library, `UMenuSettingBinderComponent`).
+- `Graphics/MenuUpscalers`: the graphics feature table types, `UMenuSettingTarget_GraphicsFeature`, `UMenuGraphicsLibrary`.
+- `Input/`: `MenuInputTypes` (devices, gamepad families, `UMenuKeyGlyphSet`), `MenuInputSubsystem` (device detection, glyphs), `MenuKeyPrompt` (`UMenuKeyPrompt`, `SMenuKeyPrompt`, `SMenuKeyGlyph`), `MenuInputModifiers` (Scale By Setting, Dead Zone By Setting).
+- `Graph/`: `StatGraph` (`UStatGraph`, `SStatGraph`), `StatGraphSources`, `MenuBenchmark` (`FMenuBenchmarkRun`, Run Benchmark node, `MenuFrameTimes`).
+- `Widgets/`: `MenuStyle` (`FMenuStyle`, `UMenuStyleAsset`), `SMenuControls` (button, switch, slider, selector, dialog, option list, drawing helpers), `SMenuSettingRow` (a setting's row, key capture), `SMenuSettingsPanel` (the whole screen), `SettingsMenu` (`USettingsMenu`, `UMenuSettingControl`, `UMenuSettingRowWidget`, `UMenuSettingsScreen`), `MenuDialog` (Show Menu Dialog), `SMenuImage`.
+- AI: `NameTBDAI/Private/NameTBDAITools_Menus.cpp`, `Resources/AI/Docs/menus.md`, a Map.md line.
+
+## Settings
+- **A setting** (`UMenuSetting`, instanced in schemas): Id (what it is saved under, what conditions and code use), Display Name, Description, Keywords (search), Preview image; **Target** (where the value goes, below; none = Saved Value), Scope (Machine / User), Apply Mode (Default = the screen's policy / Immediately / On Apply), Requires Confirmation, Requires Restart, Reapply When Changed (ids); Shown When / Enabled When conditions (+ Disabled Reason), Platforms (`Windows`, `Desktop`, `Console`, `Mobile`...), When Unavailable (Hide / Disable).
+- **Kinds:** Bool (On / Off text), Number (Min / Max / Step, Format Number / Percent / Percent Value / Multiplier, Decimals, Units, Min Text / Max Text - "Off", "Unlimited"), Choice (Options with Label, Description, Preview, Hidden Unless Current - Overall Quality's "Custom"; Wrap; Display Auto / Selector / Dropdown / Buttons), Key Binding (Mapping Name, Device, Slot Count), Action (Event / Auto-Detect Graphics / Reset Page / Reset All / Reset Key Bindings / Run Benchmark; Button Text; Confirm Text), Info (read-only text from its target).
+- **Values are text** (the save, conditions and the AI use one form): Bool "true" / "false", Number "1.5", Choice its option's Value.
+- **Conditions** (`FMenuSettingCondition`): another setting's value Equals / Not Equals / Greater / ... / Is True / Is False / Is Any Of (comma list); numbers compare as numbers. **System values**: `@ActiveUpscaler`, `@ActiveFrameGeneration`, `@ActiveLatencyReduction`, `@GPUVendor` (NVIDIA / AMD / Intel / Any), `@Platform`, `@RayTracingSupported`, `@InputDevice` (KeyboardMouse / Gamepad / Touch), `@Editing`. A condition on a setting that doesn't exist fails (its row hides).
+- **Schemas** (`UMenuSettingsSchema`, Primary Data Asset): Pages (Id, Display Name, Icon, Order, Platforms, Sections (Id, Title, Settings, Key Bindings (+ device, categories), Shown When)), Priority. Merged over the built-in pages in Priority order: a page with an existing Id adds its sections; a section with an existing Id (or title) adds its settings; a setting with an existing Id replaces it in place. Sources: the built-in pages (Include Built In Pages), Project Settings > Menus > Schemas, a Settings Menu's Extra Schemas, Register Schema at run time. Project settings also hide pages / settings by Id and set project defaults by Id. Validation: duplicate ids, missing ids.
+
+## Built-in pages (`MenuSettingsDefaults.cpp`)
+| Page | Section | Settings (Id after the page's prefix) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Gameplay (100) | General | Language (cultures the game is localized to, native names), FieldOfView (70-120°, camera manager + active camera component, reapplied on map / pawn change), CameraShake (saved) |
+| | Notifications | DoNotDisturb, NotificationSounds (the plugin's notification preferences) |
+| Video (200) | Display | WindowMode (Fullscreen / Borderless / Windowed, confirm), Resolution (the monitor's list, confirm, disabled in Borderless), VSync, FrameRateLimit (30 ... 240, Unlimited), Brightness (display gamma 1.6-3.0), HDR (when supported, confirm), HDRBrightness (nits, shown with HDR) |
+| | Upscaling & Frame Generation | Upscaler (Auto + every supported feature), UpscalerMode (the active upscaler's modes), ResolutionScale (25-100%, greyed while a mode sets it; written again when it stops), Sharpness (the upscaler's own), DLSSRayReconstruction (shown with DLSS), FrameGeneration, LatencyReduction |
+| | Quality | OverallQuality (Low-Cinematic, Custom), ViewDistance / Texture / Shadow / GlobalIllumination / Reflection / Effects / PostProcess / Foliage / Shading / AntiAliasing Quality, RenderDistance (r.ViewDistanceScale 0.5-2x), TextureFiltering (r.MaxAnisotropy), HardwareRayTracing (r.Lumen.HardwareRayTracing, shown when the RHI supports ray tracing), AutoDetect (engine hardware benchmark + recommended levels + Auto upscaler) |
+| | Camera Effects | MotionBlur, DepthOfField, Bloom, LensFlares, ChromaticAberration, FilmGrain (each its cvar on / off) |
+| | Performance | PerformanceOverlay (Off / FPS / Frame Times / Detailed), Benchmark (15 s) |
+| | System | Info: GraphicsCard, Driver, GraphicsAPI, Processor, Memory |
+| Audio (300) | Volume | Master / Music / Effects / Dialogue / UI / Voice volume (sound classes from Project Settings > Menus > Audio Channels; Master works with none - the audio device's volume), BackgroundVolume (desktop) |
+| | Output | Quality (the engine's audio quality levels, restart) |
+| Controls (400) | Mouse | MouseSensitivity, MouseInvertY (desktop) |
+| | Controller | GamepadSensitivityX / Y, GamepadInvertY, GamepadDeadZone, Vibration, VibrationStrength, AimAssist (saved), ButtonPrompts (Auto / Xbox / PlayStation / Switch / Generic) |
+| | Keyboard & Mouse Bindings / Controller Bindings | every player mappable key, by category; ResetKeyBindings |
+| Accessibility (500) | Visual | ColorBlindMode (Deuteranopia / Protanopia / Tritanopia correction), ColorBlindStrength, UIScale (75-150%), HighContrast (menus), ReduceMotion (menus, notifications, `Is Reduce Motion Enabled`), ReduceFlashing (saved) |
+| | Subtitles | Subtitles (engine), SubtitleSize, SubtitleBackground, SpeakerNames (saved) |
+| | Reading & Notifications | MenuNarration (screen reader reads the focused setting), ReadNotifications, NotificationDuration (1-10x), KeepNotifications |
+| | Input | ToggleInsteadOfHold (saved) |
+
+"Saved" settings have no target: the game reads them (Get Setting Number / Bool, a Setting Binder, the input modifiers). Ids are listed in `Resources/AI/Docs/menus.md` too.
+
+## Targets (where a value goes)
+- **Console Variable**: any cvar (Name, Also Set, Scale, Invert, Value Map), written with Game Setting priority; unavailable while the cvar doesn't exist (a plugin off). Read back (so a quality preset's changes show).
+- **Game User Settings**: Window Mode, Resolution (options from the monitor; Windowed lists convenient sizes), VSync, Frame Rate Limit, Overall Quality, the ten scalability groups, Resolution Scale, Dynamic Resolution, HDR Output / Nits (only where supported), Audio Quality. Applied (`ApplyResolutionSettings` / `ApplyNonResolutionSettings`) and saved by the engine.
+- **Sound Volume**: Channel (Master, Music...) -> the project's sound class through a settings sound mix (made at run time if the project names none); reapplied after map loads.
+- **Built-in**: Display Gamma, UI Scale (`UUserInterfaceSettings::ApplicationScale`), Color Blind Mode / Strength, Subtitles, Background Volume, Vibration / Strength (the controller's force feedback, by reflection), Reduce Motion / High Contrast / Menu Narration (plugin flags, `MenuAccessibility`), Controller Button Style, Field Of View.
+- **Notification Preference**, **Language** (cultures with game localization, saved to config), **System Info**, **Graphics Feature** (below), **Saved Value**, and **Blueprint Target** (your own: Write Value / Read Value / Can Be Used events, Use Saved Value, Reapply After Map Load).
+- C++: subclass `UMenuSettingTarget` (Is Available, Read, Write, Get Default, Get Options, Uses Saved Value, Reapply After Map Load, Writes Default On Start, Save).
+
+## The subsystem (`UMenuSettingsSubsystem`, per local player)
+- **Start:** the built-in schema, key binding contexts registered with Enhanced Input user settings, pages merged, the machine save (`NameTBD_Settings`, user 0) and the player's (`NameTBD_PlayerSettings`, platform user index) loaded; values: saved (when the target uses saved values), else the target's current value, else the default. **Only what the player changed is written on start** (an untouched cvar, volume or camera stays the game's) - except targets that must hold from the first frame (the upscaler, its mode, frame generation, latency reduction: Auto picks DLSS on RTX). A 0.25 s watch notices the player's controller arriving or changing (PIE start, map loads) and writes again what a map or pawn resets (sound mixes, force feedback, field of view), and binds the pawn-change event.
+- **Changing:** Set Setting Value (made valid; disabled settings refuse) -> the target's Write -> stored in the scope's save -> every readable target read again (a preset's effect shows) -> settings listing it in Reapply When Changed written again -> On Setting Changed for each value that changed. Restart-required settings notify once (a notification). Step Setting, Reset Setting (back to default and out of the save, so the engine decides again), Reset Page, Reset All, Get / Set All Setting Values (cloud saves, presets).
+- **Editing session** (Begin / End Editing, nesting): the snapshot Revert returns to (values, saves, keys). With the Apply Button policy, settings with Apply Mode Default wait (Get Setting Value shows them); Apply Settings commits them, starting the **confirmation** for Requires Confirmation ones: Confirmation Seconds (15) in real time (capped delta), On Confirmation Started / Ended; Confirm Settings(Keep) or the timeout reverts. Revert Settings puts values, saves and key bindings back. End Editing saves (async by default; sync on shutdown).
+- **Key bindings:** Can Rebind Keys, Get Bound Key / Default (mapping, device, slot index -> the mapping's slots of that device in slot order), Bind Key (reserved keys refused, wrong device refused, conflict policy Swap / Unbind / Allow / Refuse with a message), Unbind, Reset Key Binding / All, Find Key Conflict, display names; saved with Enhanced Input's user settings. Key binding sections list one row per mapping of the device, sorted by category (the screen puts a heading over each).
+- **Benchmark** (Start Benchmark, On Benchmark Finished, notifications) and the **performance overlay** (a Stat Graph put on the player's screen in the project's corner for Video > Performance Overlay; back after map loads).
+- **Console:** `NameTBD.Settings.List [filter]`, `NameTBD.Settings.Set <Id> <Value>`, `NameTBD.Settings.Reset [Id]`, `NameTBD.Settings.Graphics` (features: installed, supported, active, Auto's pick), `NameTBD.Benchmark [seconds]`.
+
+## Graphics features (`Graphics/MenuUpscalers`, Project Settings > Menus > Graphics Features)
+- A row per technology: Id, Kind (Upscaler / Frame Generation / Latency Reduction), Display Name, Description, Vendor, Preferred On (+50 Auto priority), **Detect Variable** (exists only with the vendor plugin), **Support Function** ("/Script/Module.Class:Function", a static bool called through reflection - no build dependency), Requires Feature, Enable / Disable Variables, Modes (Variables, Screen Percentage), Default Mode, Sharpness Variable, Requires Restart, Auto Priority. Status: installed / supported / why not ("Needs an NVIDIA graphics card").
+- **Shipped rows:** DLSS (DLAA, Quality 66.67%, Balanced 58%, Performance 50%, Ultra Performance 33.33%; `r.NGX.DLSS.Enable`, `DLSSLibrary:IsDLSSSupported`), FSR (Native AA ... Ultra Performance via `r.FidelityFX.FSR3.QualityMode`, sharpness), XeSS (Native AA, Ultra Quality Plus ... Ultra Performance via `r.XeSS.Quality`), TSR (the five modes + Custom), TAA, FXAA, Off; DLSS Frame Generation (`r.Streamline.DLSSG.Enable`, `StreamlineLibraryDLSSG:IsDLSSGSupported`), FSR Frame Generation (needs FSR), XeSS Frame Generation; NVIDIA Reflex (On, On + Boost), AMD Anti-Lag 2, Intel XeLL.
+- Applying a feature turns the rest of its kind off, sets its enable variables, the mode's variables and its screen percentage; what is active is remembered (Get Active Graphics Feature / Mode, `@ActiveUpscaler`). Auto = the supported upscaler with the highest priority on this vendor.
+
+## Input (`Input/`)
+- **Menu Input Subsystem** (per local player): a Slate pre-processor sees every key, stick, mouse move and touch (never takes them) for this player's Slate user; switches Keyboard & Mouse / Gamepad / Touch with thresholds (Mouse Switch Distance 6 px, Stick Switch Threshold 0.4); the gamepad family from the hardware name (`FInputDeviceScope`; Project Settings Gamepad Hardware map, contains-match) or the platform; the Button Prompts setting overrides. Get Key For Action (the player's mapping, Enhanced Input `QueryKeysMappedToAction`) and Get Key Glyph (Key Glyph Sets per family + keyboard, else a family label: Cross / Circle / Square / Triangle, L1, ZL...). On Input Device Changed.
+- **Menu Key Prompt** (palette NameTBD): Input Action or Keyboard / Gamepad Key, Show Device (Current / KBM / Gamepad), Label, Hide When Unbound (and on touch), Key Cap style (height, font, colours, corner), clickable (On Prompt Clicked), hold progress; refreshes on device and binding changes.
+- **Input modifiers:** Scale By Setting (sensitivity X / Y settings, invert X / Y settings, base scale) and Dead Zone By Setting (radial / axial, setting + default), read every frame.
+- **Rebinding UI:** a row's slots (primary / secondary; one for gamepad), Accept or click to capture ("Press a key..."), a capture pre-processor consumes the next key / mouse button / wheel for the player (Escape, or Menu on a pad row, cancels; the wrong device says so and keeps waiting; Key Capture Timeout 8 s), Delete / right-click unbinds, messages for swaps and refusals.
+
+## Graph and benchmark (`Graph/`)
+- **Stat Graph** (palette NameTBD): Series (Label, instanced Source, Color, Style Line / Area / Bars, Thickness, Graphed, Listed, Decimals); sampling in real time (History Seconds, Sample Interval 0 = every frame, Readout Seconds); range Auto From Zero / Auto / Fixed (eased, readable ceilings, Minimum Span); Reference Lines; headline value; legend with current / average / min-max / 1% low (or high, for ms); threshold colours (fps 60 / 30, ms 16.7 / 33.3); background, corner radius, grid, axis labels, fonts. Presets: Compact FPS, FPS, Frame Times, Detailed, Memory, Network. Push Value, Add Series, Clear, Pause, Get Series Stats. Live in the designer.
+- **Sources:** Frame Rate, Frame Time, Thread Time (Game / Render / RHI / GPU - stat unit's numbers), Memory (used physical / virtual, available), Console Variable, Ping, Manual, and Blueprint sources (Sample event).
+- **Benchmark:** `FMenuBenchmarkRun` (real time, warm-up), Run Benchmark async node, Video > Benchmark, `NameTBD.Benchmark`: frames, average fps, 1% and 0.1% lows, min / max, average and 99th percentile frame time, per-thread averages, hitches (> 2.5x the average), CSV per frame with a summary in Saved/Benchmarks.
+
+## Screens and widgets (`Widgets/`)
+- **Menu Style** (`UMenuStyleAsset` data asset; `FMenuStyle`): Preset (Simple, Light, Glass, Minimal, Console, High Contrast), Colors + High Contrast Colors (used while High Contrast Menus is on), fonts (title, tab, section, label, value, description, hint, button), layout (screen padding, content max width, corner radius, row height / padding / spacing, section spacing, value width, description width, tab spacing, outline and focus outline widths), look (tab style Underline / Pills / Boxed, tab icons, bool as Switch / Selector, Selector Max Options, pips, description panel, search, footer hints, modified dot, focus bar, background image, background blur, key caps), motion (Motion, slide pages, page transition seconds), sounds (navigate, change, accept, back, tab, error), custom rows per kind. Edits reach every screen using it live (`OnStyleChanged`; Notify Style Changed at run time). Screens without one use Project Settings > Menus > Default Style, else Simple.
+- **Settings Menu** (palette NameTBD, `USettingsMenu`): Style Asset, Pages (filter / order), Initial Page, Extra Schemas, Title, Apply Policy (Instant / Apply Button), Confirm Unsaved On Back, Back / Reset prompts, Focus On Show, keys (previous / next tab LB / RB, Q / E; apply X, F; reset Y, R; back B, Esc), texts; On Back, On Page Changed, On Setting Focused; Open / Close Session, Set Page, Next / Previous Page, Apply / Revert / Reset Current Page, Request Back, Focus First Setting / Setting, Set Style Asset, Set Search Text, Refresh. In the designer it shows the real pages with preview values.
+- The screen (`SMenuSettingsPanel`): title, search (across pages, keywords), tabs with the prompts that change them, sections with headings, key binding category headings, rows, a description panel (name, current / default, option preview image, description, option description, why it is disabled, restart / confirmation notes; hidden under 1100 px), footer prompts (Reset to Defaults, Revert Changes, Apply, Back - clickable, for the device in use), dialogs (keep display changes with a countdown, unsaved changes Apply / Discard / Cancel, confirmations, dropdown lists), page transitions (fade, slide; Reduce Motion: fade only), sounds (real-time throttled), narration (focused row, value changes, pages, dialogs). Shown rows are recomputed after each change (HDR on shows HDR Brightness) keeping focus.
+- **Rows** (`SMenuSettingRow`): switch or selector (bools), slider with value (numbers), selector with arrows and pips / dropdown / segmented buttons (choices), key slots, action button, read-only value; hover / focus highlight with an accent bar and outline, a modified dot, messages under the name. Left / right step, Accept toggles / opens / captures / runs; disabled rows stay focusable.
+- **Setting Control** (palette NameTBD): one setting's row anywhere. **Menu Setting Row Widget**: your own row in UMG (Label / Value / Description Text parts filled; On Setting Assigned / Refreshed; Set Value, Step, Reset To Default, Run Action) - for a whole kind via the style's Custom Rows, or placed by hand with a Setting Id. **Menu Settings Screen**: a User Widget parent implementing the Menu Screen Interface around a Settings Menu (session on open / close, focus, Back through the menu then closing itself through the Menu Manager).
+- **Show Menu Dialog** (async node): title, body, buttons (Primary / Secondary / Subtle), default and cancel buttons, optional timeout with a countdown; on the player's screen above everything, focus restored after.
+
+## Menu Manager (upgraded)
+- Kept: screens by gameplay tag (widget class, input context, pre-warm, Z order, pause in standalone, Closes Screens, toggle action), local-only contract, mapping contexts per input context.
+- **New per screen** (all default to the old behaviour): Input Mode (Default / UI Only with the screen focused / Game And UI), Screen Mapping Context (while top), Hide Cursor With Gamepad, Close On Back, Focus On Open (None / Screen / Named Widget) + Restore Focus (focus put back on the screen below when the top one closes, also on picking up a pad with nothing focused), Async Load (opens when the class has streamed in; Is Menu Loading; closing cancels), Close Delay (stays visible, not hit-testable, for its exit animation), Return To Closed Screens (Settings opened from Pause goes back to Pause; not while Close All), Suppress Notifications (Freeze / Hold / Drop while open).
+- **Back:** Request Back - the top screen's new interface event On Back Requested may handle it (a sub-page, a dialog, unsaved changes); else it closes when Close On Back; with nothing open, Back Opens Screen (the pause menu). The Close Top Screen Action goes through it. Find Menu Manager (controller, pawn, player state), Find Screen Tag, Close Screen Widget.
+
+## AI Assistant
+- `create_settings_menu` {name, tabs, folder, title, style, style_asset, colors, style_props, apply_policy}: a `WBP_` Menu Settings Screen with a Settings Menu filling it (GUIDs given, compiled), a `DA_<Name>_Style` Menu Style (preset + colours + fields), and for tabs that aren't built-in a `DA_<Name>_Settings` schema with those pages. The acceptance prompt ("tabs: controls, video, audio and accessibility, simple style bound to a data asset") is one call.
+- `add_menu_settings` {schema, folder, page, section, settings, menu}: settings from specs (type, range, format, options, action, target {type: cvar / game_user_setting / built_in / sound / notification / graphics / language / saved, ...fields}, scope, apply, restart / confirmation, conditions with symbols, keywords, props) into a schema (made if needed; same id replaces), optionally listed in a menu's Extra Schemas (and its page added to its filter).
+- `list_menu_settings` (read): pages, sections, setting ids and kinds, graphics features with their status, style presets.
+
+## Beyond the request (production expectations added)
+- Settings platform: data-driven schemas merged over built-in pages, replace / hide by id, project defaults, platform filters, availability (hidden or greyed with the reason), conditions on other settings and system values, dependencies (reapply), machine vs per-player saves (split screen), only-changed-values written, Apply / Revert / Reset Page / Reset All, keep-display-changes countdown, restart-required notice, cloud-save import / export, console commands, validation.
+- Graphics: Auto upscaler per vendor, every UE5 AA method, DLAA / Native AA, Ray Reconstruction, frame generation, latency reduction, sharpness, resolution scale that steps aside for upscaler modes, hardware benchmark auto-detect, HDR with peak brightness, frame rate limit, texture filtering, hardware ray tracing, camera effects toggles, system info, performance overlay, benchmark with CSV.
+- Accessibility beyond the floor: colour blindness filters with strength, UI scale, high contrast menus (a separate palette), reduce motion wired through menus and notifications, menu narration through the screen reader, notification time / keep-until-closed / read-aloud, subtitles options, flashing reduction, toggle instead of hold, field of view and camera shake.
+- Input: device switching with thresholds, gamepad family detection and override, glyph sets, key prompts, rebinding with conflict policies, reserved keys, capture timeout, sensitivity / invert / dead zone modifiers, cursor and focus following the device.
+- Screens: one complete Settings Menu with search, description panel, footer prompts, dialogs, sounds, transitions, live style asset, custom UMG rows, single Setting Controls, Menu Settings Screen, Show Menu Dialog, Setting Binder component for any property.
+- Menu Manager: Back routing with screens handling it, back-opens-pause, UI-only input with focus, screen mapping contexts, focus memory, async loading, exit animations, return-to-previous, notification suppression.
+
+## Decisions made without asking
+- **Settings in schemas + a per-player subsystem**, not a menu-owned store: any widget, Blueprint or system reads the same values; the built-in pages are made in code so they need no asset and stay current with the plugin.
+- **Vendor technology by console variables and reflection**, never a build dependency: the plugin builds with none of the vendor plugins installed; a missing plugin hides its options; new versions are table rows. The shipped variable names are the vendors' documented ones as known; a wrong one only hides that option.
+- **Untouched settings are never written** (except the upscaler family): the project's scalability, device profiles and inis keep deciding until the player changes something; Reset returns a setting to that state.
+- **Instant policy by default** (console standard; display changes still confirm), Apply Button available per screen.
+- **Real time** for confirmation countdowns, benchmark, graphs and dialog timeouts (menus are often shown paused); the panel's sounds are throttled in real time because the shared UI sound player throttles on world time, which stops while paused.
+- **Machine scope** for display, graphics, audio, colour blindness and UI scale (one screen, one audio device); **user scope** for controls, accessibility and gameplay.
+- Menu Manager additions default to the old behaviour (the project rule); the pause / multiplayer contract is unchanged.
+- Key bindings stay in Enhanced Input's own save (its user settings), not the plugin's.
+- The Menu Settings Screen's On Back Requested always reports handled: the menu decides, and closes itself through the manager.
+
+## Still open
